course: dictionary
lesson: 7492
title: Postage: the cost of sending
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Postage is the money you pay to send a letter or parcel by post. It is part of the price when you buy something online. «The Penny Black of 1840 in Britain was the first postage stamp you stick on a letter.» So postage is also the stamp that shows the sender has paid.
explain: In a money problem, add postage to the price to find the total. If a game costs £12 and postage is £3, then the total is £12 + £3 = £15. Always check: does your answer make sense? The total must be more than the price alone.
explain: Postage depends on weight and size. A heavier parcel usually costs more to send. In Britain people say «P&P» for postage and packing, and in the USA they often say shipping instead.
explain: Be careful with money for postage. «Fake giveaways promise expensive prizes to strangers and often ask for "postage" money or private details.» A real company will not ask a stranger to pay for a prize. If someone asks you for postage money, tell a grown-up.
fact: Postage is the money you pay to send a letter or parcel by post.
fact: Postage is also the stamp or mark on a letter that shows it has been paid for.
fact: «The Penny Black» was the first postage stamp, from Britain in 1840.
fact: In maths money problems, total = price + postage.
fact: Heavier and bigger parcels usually cost more postage.
exercise: A game costs £12 and the postage is £3. What is the total price? | £12 | *£15 | £36 | £9
exercise: Sam wants to post a heavy parcel. What will happen to the postage? | It will go down, because it is heavy | *It will cost more, because heavier parcels cost more | It will be free, because it is heavy | It will stay the same for every weight
exercise: What is a postage stamp? | A tiny letter sent by post | *A mark on a letter showing the postage has been paid | A type of parcel box | A prize from a giveaway
test: «The sender paid a penny in advance, whatever the distance.» What does in advance mean? | Never | After the letter arrived | Only if the letter was far away | *Before sending
test: Which short form is used in the UK for postage and packing? | *P&P | BBC | USA | ETA
exam: A fake giveaway asks you to pay postage to get a prize. What should you do? | Send your bank details so they can post the prize | *Do not pay, and tell a grown-up because it may be a scam | Pay straight away, because the prize is worth it | Share the offer with all your friends so they can pay too
